# mkfs.pdxfs — caps.decl
#
# Wave: R53 (design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md §2.1 + §3 + §9.1, paideia-os
# repo). mkfs.pdxfs is a standalone CLI tool (a ring-3 ELF with its own
# `_start`, not a shared library like libpdx-volume/libpdx-audit): it
# performs its own syscalls directly (self-contained inlined-syscall
# pattern, matching src/user/true.pdx / cat.pdx / mkdir.pdx in the
# paideia-os monorepo) rather than delegating every kernel touch to a
# linked library.
#
# consumed_kinds (kernel-owned; paideia-os repo):
#
#   KIND_USER              = 0x190  (src/kernel/core/cap/kind_user.pdx)
#     -- invoker identity, consumed for audit attribution
#        (`invoker_user` field of PdxFsFormatRecord@0.1, §3.5) and for
#        the sig-key-owner check at M3-002. Not dereferenced by any M1
#        code path -- M1 never journals and never signs.
#
#   KIND_PDXFS_FILE         = 0x195  (src/kernel/core/cap/kind_pdxfs_file.pdx)
#     -- one cap per invocation when <target> resolves to a filesystem
#        path (§3.2 "File-backed path"). Opened read+write; if the
#        target does not exist, mkfs creates it (parent-directory write
#        authority required) and truncates to --size= (default 128 MiB).
#        Not opened by any M1 code path -- M1's --dry-run path never
#        calls sys_open; it only inspects <target>'s STRING form (does
#        it start with `/`, `~`, `.`, or `cap:blkdev:`) to decide which
#        branch to print, per target.pdx's M1 classify-only stub.
#
#        M2 (src/format.pdx's mkfs_format_run, src/refusal.pdx's
#        mkfs_refuse_check) DOES now call sys_open/sys_read/sys_write/
#        sys_close for real against a file-backed target -- but as a
#        BARE syscall on the raw path string, not as a cap-invoke
#        against a minted KIND_PDXFS_FILE row. This KIND remains
#        undeclared-in-practice at M2: no code path in this repo mints,
#        holds, or narrows one. Whether the real write pipeline should
#        route through a KIND_PDXFS_FILE cap instead of bare syscalls is
#        an open question for a later milestone (mount.pdxfs's own
#        design already assumes cap-mediated access post-mount; whether
#        mkfs, which runs pre-mount against a not-yet-formatted target,
#        needs the same is unresolved -- flagged in
#        design/architecture.md §10 for main/osarch).
#
#   KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE       = placeholder, 0x198..0x19F band per
#     volume-tooling-ux.md §2.1 / §12 coordination point 1 (osarch, R51)
#     -- consumed when <target> resolves to a `cap:blkdev:` URI (§3.2
#        "Device-cap URI"). The tool holds an `open+write+flush+query`
#        sub-cap, narrowed via a future libpdx-volume helper once one
#        exists for KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE (libpdx-volume's own M1 landing
#        only narrows KIND_VOLUME, not KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE directly --
#        see libpdx-volume design/architecture.md §5).
#
#     NAMING GAP flagged for main (mirrors the discrepancy libpdx-volume's
#     own caps.decl / design/architecture.md §4 flags for
#     KIND_PDXFS_MOUNT_TABLE): the kernel-landed block-device kind as of
#     this M1 landing is `KIND_BLKDEV = 0x42`
#     (src/kernel/core/cap/kind_blkdev.pdx), NOT a kind at ordinal
#     0x198..0x19F. `KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE` at the 0x198..0x19F band is this
#     design doc's own placeholder name for a not-yet-landed R51 osarch
#     kind distinct from the existing KIND_BLKDEV. This M1 landing
#     declares the PLACEHOLDER name the design doc's own issue list uses
#     (`mkfs.pdxfs.M1-001 ... KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE placeholder ...`) rather
#     than silently substituting the existing KIND_BLKDEV=0x42, since the
#     two may not be interchangeable (KIND_BLKDEV's tail shape and rights
#     band have not been audited against this design doc's
#     open+write+flush+query op list). Confirm with osarch before
#     mkfs.pdxfs.M3-001 (device-cap target path) implements a real mint/
#     narrow call against either kind.
#
#   KIND_SIG_KEY            = 0x1A3  (src/kernel/core/cap/kind_sig_key.pdx)
#     -- placeholder at M1: the signing key material used to sign the
#        superblock byte range [0, 696) at M3-002
#        (libpdx-volume.pdxb_sign_superblock). Not referenced by any M1
#        function; M1's --dry-run record always reports `signed: false`
#        (no --sig-key parsing beyond storing the raw argv pointer in
#        ParsedArgv.sig_key_path_ptr -- see src/argv.pdx).
#
#   KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT       = 5 (base kind, R20b) -- the semantic-pipe
#     stdin/stdout surface. Per design/tooling/r49-r50-plan.md §3.2, a
#     semantic pipe is "a subclass of KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT (base kind 5)
#     carrying a schema handle alongside the byte stream." Declared here
#     as a placeholder per mkfs.pdxfs.M1-001's own issue text
#     ("semantic-pipe stdin/stdout kinds"); NOT bound or invoked by any
#     M1 code. M1's stdout is a plain `sys_write(1, ...)` of a
#     human-readable line (src/format_record.pdx); the schema-typed
#     framing over a bound KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT lands at
#     mkfs.pdxfs.M3-003 once libpdx-semantic-pipe (or an equivalent) is
#     linkable -- see design/architecture.md §4 for the deferral note.
#
#   KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL    = 0x191 -- referenced by volume-tooling-ux.md
#     §2.1 for the device-cap elevate path (M3-005). Not declared as a
#     consumed kind at M1: no code path in this landing calls
#     libpdx-elevate (which itself has not been located under
#     paideia-satellites/ as of this landing -- see design/architecture.md
#     §3 for the libpdx-argv/libpdx-elevate availability note).
#
# declares_output_schemas: none bound at M1. `PdxFsFormatRecord@0.1`'s
# FIELD SHAPE is fixed by design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md §3.5 and
# this M1 landing's --dry-run path prints a line-based textual rendering
# of exactly four of its fields (target, label, journal_size, dry_run --
# see src/format_record.pdx module header for which fields M1 omits and
# why). The typed schema-registry binding (BLAKE3-truncated fingerprint
# constant, semantic-pipe framing) is owned by mkfs.pdxfs.M3-003 per
# volume-tooling-ux.md §7.4, not this issue.
#
# M1 landing status (see STATUS.md): this repo performed exactly two
# syscalls at M1 -- `sys_write` (SC+ ID 1, to fd 1 for the dry-run record
# and fd 2 for error diagnostics) and `sys_exit` (SC+ ID 60). No
# sys_open, no sys_svc_lookup, no sys_ipc_send, no cap-invoke of any
# kind -- every KIND above is declared for the SHAPE this tool's future
# milestones consume, per the same "typed-against, not yet touched"
# posture libpdx-volume's own M1 caps.decl documents for its stub
# functions.
#
# M2 landing status (see STATUS.md, design/architecture.md §9): the
# real file-target write pipeline (src/format.pdx) and non-blank
# refusal gate (src/refusal.pdx) add four more syscalls, all against a
# raw filesystem path -- `sys_open` (SC+ ID 2, O_RDONLY for the refusal
# gate's peek read, O_CREAT|O_WRONLY|O_TRUNC for the real format
# write), `sys_read` (SC+ ID 0, the refusal gate's 4-byte magic peek),
# `sys_write` (SC+ ID 1, now also used for the superblock/inode-table/
# bitmap/journal byte payloads, not just diagnostic text), and
# `sys_close` (SC+ ID 3). All four operate directly on the bare
# filesystem path string from argv -- none of them are cap-invokes, and
# none of the KIND_PDXFS_FILE / KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE / KIND_SIG_KEY /
# KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT / KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL kinds above are minted,
# looked up, or otherwise touched by any M2 code path -- the "typed-
# against, not yet touched" posture above is unchanged for every KIND
# except KIND_USER, which M2 also does not touch (invoker attribution
# is still mkfs.pdxfs.M3-004, audit integration).
#
# M3 landing status (see STATUS.md, design/architecture.md §11): four
# new satellite-library links, one KIND naming resolution, no new
# syscalls of this repo's own.
#
# consumed_satellite_libs (all cross-repo bare-label `call`s, the same
# mechanism M2's `pdxb_encode_superblock` call already used -- see
# design/architecture.md §9.6):
#
#   libpdx-volume (@ commit 6f18957, M3) -- `pdxb_sign_superblock`
#     (src/format.pdx's mkfs_format_run, #9). REAL: signs every
#     file-target superblock in place with a PLACEHOLDER all-zero
#     32-byte seed (real seed-loading needs a `libpdx-key`-equivalent
#     that does not exist yet -- see src/format.pdx's own module
#     header). Does NOT touch KIND_SIG_KEY (0x1A3, still a placeholder
#     per M1 -- confirmed by libpdx-volume's own architecture.md §8.2
#     that KIND_SIG_KEY is a public-key handle, not a private seed;
#     `pdxb_sign_superblock`'s `seed_ptr` argument is a raw pointer, not
#     a cap slot).
#
#   libpdx-audit (@0.2, commit bfc63a5) -- `AuditClient::audit_begin`,
#     `AuditClient::audit_commit` (src/audit_wire.pdx, #11). REAL calls
#     (real IPC send attempts), but the daemon-side dispatch is
#     confirmed STUBBED (libpdx-audit's own STATUS.md:69-70:
#     `audit_journal_broker_dispatch` returns `AJB_DISPATCH_STUB`) --
#     every call in this landing may therefore no-op at the daemon, per
#     this issue's own forgiving-posture instruction. No retain-forever
#     UEJ_KIND exists in libpdx-audit @0.2 (grepped, confirmed absent) --
#     src/audit_wire.pdx's own module header flags this for main.
#
#   libpdx-elevate (4844 LOC, mature) -- NOT actually called for a real
#     elevation decision (src/elevate_wire.pdx, #12): this library's
#     real API (`elevate_client_acquire`/`elevate_client_require`) needs
#     a `parent_ep_slot` broker-endpoint cap this repo does not hold
#     (KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL = 0x191, still the M1 placeholder, unchanged
#     by this landing -- no code path in this repo mints or acquires
#     one). `mkfs_elev_require_device_write` is therefore a fail-closed
#     stub returning DENY unconditionally -- see that file's own module
#     header for the full mismatch between this issue's assumed API
#     shape and libpdx-elevate's real one.
#
#   libpdx-semantic-pipe (v1.0.0, real + released) -- NOT linked
#     (src/pipe_wire.pdx, #10): confirmed via GitHub issue
#     paideia-os#2000 that `Registry::bind_by_name` is inert (the
#     backing `svc.schema-registry` service does not exist yet, so
#     `bind_by_name` always returns 304/LOOKUP_FAIL). Per this issue's
#     own fallback instruction, every PdxFsFormatRecord@0.1 this repo
#     emits remains the M1/M2 line-based `sys_write(1, ...)` rendering,
#     now preceded by one documented deferral header line.
#
# KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE naming gap RESOLVED (src/target.pdx's own module
# header has the full write-up): `design/hardware/nvme-ahci-tail-
# milestones.md` §3.1 (paideia-os) confirms `KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE` is
# purely a doc-readability alias for the already-landed
# `KIND_BLKDEV = 0x42` -- there is no separate kind at the previously
# flagged 0x198..0x19F band. What remains unresolved is the ABSENCE of
# any cap-introspection (`sys_cap_query`, planned at R13, never
# implemented) or cap-narrowing (`cap_narrow`/`sys_cap_narrow`, does not
# exist anywhere in this kernel) primitive -- `src/target.pdx`'s
# `mkfs_dev_parse_slot` (#8) parses a device-cap slot number for real,
# but validating that slot's kind and narrowing it to write-only both
# remain documented STUBs for exactly this reason, not because the
# KIND name itself is still ambiguous.
